{"id":"mahabharata-3-165","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":165,"title":"पञ्चषष्ट्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 165 · Arjuna sets out against the Nivatakavachas","summary":{"en":"Indra gives Arjuna his own diadem, armour and the conch Devadatta, and Matali drives him in the celestial chariot to the city of the Nivatakavacha demons, who live in the depths of the ocean.","kn":"ಇಂದ್ರನು ಅರ್ಜುನನಿಗೆ ತನ್ನ ಕಿರೀಟ, ಕವಚ, ದೇವದತ್ತ ಶಂಖವನ್ನು ನೀಡುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಮಾತಲಿ ದಿವ್ಯರಥದಲ್ಲಿ ಸಮುದ್ರದಾಳದಲ್ಲಿ ವಾಸಿಸುವ ನಿವಾತಕವಚ ದಾನವರ ನಗರಕ್ಕೆ ಅವನನ್ನು ಕರೆದೊಯ್ಯುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"इन्द्र अर्जुन को अपना किरीट, कवच और देवदत्त शंख देते हैं, और मातलि उन्हें दिव्य रथ में समुद्र की गहराई में रहने वाले निवातकवच दानवों की नगरी ले जाते हैं।","te":"ఇంద్రుడు అర్జునునికి తన కిరీటం, కవచం, దేవదత్త శంఖం ఇస్తాడు; మాతలి దివ్యరథంలో సముద్రపు లోతుల్లో నివసించే నివాతకవచ దానవుల నగరానికి అతనిని తీసుకువెళ్తాడు.","ta":"இந்திரன் அர்ஜுனனுக்குத் தன் கிரீடம், கவசம், தேவதத்த சங்கு ஆகியவற்றை அளிக்க, மாதலி தெய்வீகத் தேரில் கடலின் ஆழத்தில் வாழும் நிவாதகவச அசுரர்களின் நகருக்கு அவனை அழைத்துச் செல்கிறான்.","ml":"ഇന്ദ്രൻ തന്റെ കിരീടവും കവചവും ദേവദത്തം എന്ന ശംഖും അർജുനന് നൽകുന്നു; സമുദ്രത്തിന്റെ ആഴത്തിൽ വസിക്കുന്ന നിവാതകവച രാക്ഷസരുടെ നഗരത്തിലേക്ക് മാതലി ദിവ്യരഥം തെളിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.165; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"यक्षयुद्धपर्व","titleEn":"Yakshayuddha Parva (Battle with the Yakshas)","verses":[{"text":"अर्जुन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"कृतास्त्रमभिविश्वस्तमथ मां हरिवाहनः ।\nसंस्पृश्य मूर्ध्नि पाणिभ्यामिदं वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When I had mastered the weapons and he trusted me, Indra, whose steeds are the bay horses, laid both hands on my head and spoke these words."}},{"n":2,"text":"न त्वमद्य युधा जेतुं शक्यः सुरगणैरपि ।\nकिं पुनर्मानुषे लोके मानुषैरकृतात्मभिः ।\nअप्रमेयोऽप्रधृष्यश्च युद्धेष्वप्रतिमस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Today not even the hosts of gods could defeat you in battle, still less men in the human world, whose minds are untrained. You are immeasurable, unassailable, and without an equal in war.\""}},{"n":3,"text":"अथाब्रवीत्पुनर्देवः संप्रहृष्टतनूरुहः ।\nअस्त्रयुद्धे समो वीर न ते कश्चिद्भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The god, the hairs of his body bristling with joy, said again: \"Hero, no one will match you in the fighting with divine weapons."}},{"n":4,"text":"अप्रमत्तः सदा दक्षः सत्यवादी जितेन्द्रियः ।\nब्रह्मण्यश्चास्त्रविच्चासि शूरश्चासि कुरूद्वह ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are always alert, skilled, truthful and master of your senses, devoted to brahmins and learned in weapons, and brave, O best of the Kurus."}},{"n":5,"text":"अस्त्राणि समवाप्तानि त्वया दश च पञ्च च ।\nपञ्चभिर्विधिभिः पार्थ न त्वया विद्यते समः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You have gained the fifteen weapons, son of Pritha, and in the five modes of using them you have no equal."}},{"n":6,"text":"प्रयोगमुपसंहारमावृत्तिं च धनंजय ।\nप्रायश्चित्तं च वेत्थ त्वं प्रतिघातं च सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhananjaya, you know how to hurl a weapon, how to withdraw it, how to repeat it, how to atone for its misuse, and how to counter it, in every way."}},{"n":7,"text":"तव गुर्वर्थकालोऽयमुपपन्नः परंतप ।\nप्रतिजानीष्व तं कर्तुमतो वेत्स्याम्यहं परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Now the time has come for you to pay your teacher's fee, scourge of foes. Promise to do it, and then I will tell you what it is.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"ततोऽहमब्रुवं राजन्देवराजमिदं वचः ।\nविषह्यं चेन्मया कर्तुं कृतमेव निबोध तत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O king, I said this to the king of the gods: \"If I am able to do it, consider it already done.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"ततो मामब्रवीद्राजन्प्रहस्य बलवृत्रहा ।\nनाविषह्यं तवाद्यास्ति त्रिषु लोकेषु किंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the mighty slayer of Vritra laughed and said to me, \"There is nothing in the three worlds that you cannot manage today."}},{"n":10,"text":"निवातकवचा नाम दानवा मम शत्रवः ।\nसमुद्रकुक्षिमाश्रित्य दुर्गे प्रतिवसन्त्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"There are danavas called the Nivatakavachas, my enemies, who live in a fortress in the depths of the ocean."}},{"n":11,"text":"तिस्रः कोट्यः समाख्यातास्तुल्यरूपबलप्रभाः ।\nतांस्तत्र जहि कौन्तेय गुर्वर्थस्ते भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"They are said to number three crores, all equal in form, strength and splendor. Kill them there, son of Kunti, and that will be your teacher's fee.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"ततो मातलिसंयुक्तं मयूरसमरोमभिः ।\nहयैरुपेतं प्रादान्मे रथं दिव्यं महाप्रभम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he gave me a great shining divine chariot, driven by Matali and drawn by horses with hair like peacock feathers."}},{"n":13,"text":"बबन्ध चैव मे मूर्ध्नि किरीटमिदमुत्तमम् ।\nस्वरूपसदृशं चैव प्रादादङ्गविभूषणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He bound on my head this excellent diadem, and gave me ornaments for my limbs that suited my own form."}},{"n":14,"text":"अभेद्यं कवचं चेदं स्पर्शरूपवदुत्तमम् ।\nअजरां ज्यामिमां चापि गाण्डीवे समयोजयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He also gave me this impenetrable armor, excellent to the touch, and fitted an ageless bowstring to the Gandiva."}},{"n":15,"text":"ततः प्रायामहं तेन स्यन्दनेन विराजता ।\nयेनाजयद्देवपतिर्बलिं वैरोचनिं पुरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then I set out in that splendid chariot, with which the lord of the gods once conquered Bali, son of Virochana."}},{"n":16,"text":"ततो देवाः सर्व एव तेन घोषेण बोधितः ।\nमन्वाना देवराजं मां समाजग्मुर्विशां पते ।\nदृष्ट्वा च मामपृच्छन्त किं करिष्यसि फल्गुन ॥","meaning":{"en":"At its rumble all the gods were roused, and thinking me to be Indra they gathered round, O lord of men. Seeing me, they asked, \"What will you do, Phalguna?\""}},{"n":17,"text":"तानब्रुवं यथाभूतमिदं कर्तास्मि संयुगे ।\nनिवातकवचानां तु प्रस्थितं मां वधैषिणम् ।\nनिबोधत महाभागाः शिवं चाशास्त मेऽनघाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I told them truly what I was going to do in battle: \"I have set out to kill the Nivatakavachas. Mark this, great ones, and wish me well, sinless ones.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"तुष्टुवुर्मां प्रसन्नास्ते यथा देवं पुरंदरम् ।\nरथेनानेन मघवा जितवाञ्शम्बरं युधि ।\nनमुचिं बलवृत्रौ च प्रह्लादनरकावपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pleased, they praised me as they would praise the god Indra: \"With this chariot Indra conquered Shambara in battle, and Namuchi, Bala and Vritra, and also Prahlada and Naraka."}},{"n":19,"text":"बहूनि च सहस्राणि प्रयुतान्यर्बुदानि च ।\nरथेनानेन दैत्यानां जितवान्मघवान्युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"With this chariot Indra defeated many thousands, tens of lakhs and crores of the daityas in battle."}},{"n":20,"text":"त्वमप्येतेन कौन्तेय निवातकवचान्रणे ।\nविजेता युधि विक्रम्य पुरेव मघवान्वशी ॥","meaning":{"en":"You too, son of Kunti, with this chariot will conquer the Nivatakavachas in the fight by your valor, as the self-controlled Indra did before."}},{"n":21,"text":"अयं च शङ्खप्रवरो येन जेतासि दानवान् ।\nअनेन विजिता लोकाः शक्रेणापि महात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"And here is the finest conch, with which you will defeat the danavas; with it great Indra too won the worlds.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"प्रदीयमानं देवैस्तु देवदत्तं जलोद्भवम् ।\nप्रत्यगृह्णं जयायैनं स्तूयमानस्तदामरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The gods were offering me the water-born conch Devadatta, and while the immortals praised me I accepted it for victory."}},{"n":23,"text":"स शङ्खी कवची बाणी प्रगृहीतशरासनः ।\nदानवालयमत्युग्रं प्रयातोऽस्मि युयुत्सया ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, with conch, armor, arrows and bow in hand, I went eager to fight toward the terrible dwelling of the danavas."}}]}]}